# Qwen4Exp precision switches — ported from Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx (ampere)
# New file vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/precision.py ships whole (see this
# repo). This diff is the two hooks: Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock.__init__ gains
# apply_router_precision(self.gate); Qwen4ExpMTP.__init__ builds its
# pre_fc_norm_hidden via the mtp_hidden_norm factory.
#
# Activation (run-qwen38fn.sh):
#   ROUTER_FP32=1      VLLM_QWEN4_ROUTER_FP32 -> cuBLAS bf16xbf16->fp32 router
#                      logits (GateLinear tier 5; works on sm80, unlike the
#                      SM90+ tiers). Fewer exact ties + matches the bf16
#                      reference which casts router logits to fp32 before topk.
#   MTP_PER_STREAM=0   VLLM_QWEN4_MTP_PER_STREAM_NORM — per-stream MTP hidden
#                      norm. OFF: A/B on this checkpoint showed spec-decode
#                      acceptance 48.4% vs 51.1% base (draft calibrated with
#                      the flat norm; upstream default OFF too).
#
# Already on in this fork (no port needed): VLLM_MOE_SKIP_PADDING=1 (envs.py
# default) routes CUDA-graph padding rows to no expert via FusedTopKRouter /
# ops.topk_*(is_padding=...); model_runner fills forward_context.is_padding.
# moe_align determinism (their align.py): deferred — our Marlin MoE computes
# each token row independently, so intra-expert rank order is numerically inert
# (the upstream atomic ordering mattered in their Triton fused-experts stack).
#
# A/B 2026-10-24 (same 3-boot suite: determinism battery + 4-way code battery
# + /metrics): base 51.05% accept / 82.0 tok-per-req; router-fp32 50.42% /
# 79.6 (within boot noise); per-stream 48.43% -> rejected.
